{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Therefore</b> — He mentioned that the souls of the wicked will perish, and he mentioned their seed in this world; therefore the word לא יקומו, whose meaning is 'they will stand.'" "<b>And the meaning of 'in the judgment'</b> — like: 'all the deed of the Elohim he will bring in judgment' (Ecclesiastes 3:17), and 'a house is opened in judgment' (Proverbs 21:9), to indicate lack of knowledge, in the manner of 'in the heavens, YHWH; in the heavens, Your faithfulness' (Psalms 89:3) — because it is the day of judgment for every single day, or for every person at his death." "<b>And the meaning of 'in the congregation of the righteous'</b> — because their joining together is good for all of them, the opposite of the joining of the wicked."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:00.319126891Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}